#. Description of the plugin
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php
msgid "Blocks or risk-scores listing submissions containing blocked words, phrases, regex patterns, phone numbers, email addresses, website URLs, duplicate content or AI-flagged text and photos, with a per-vendor submission limit, a verified-vendor bypass, and a Moderation score column and meta box in the dashboard. Configure under HivePress → Settings → Listings → Automated Moderation."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:184
msgid "Block submission"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:186
msgid "Add to risk score"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:187
msgid "Add to risk score (set a Risk Threshold below first)"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:206
msgid "Automated Moderation"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:207
msgid "Checks each listing as it is submitted or edited on your site, and either refuses it or holds it as Pending under Listings in the WordPress dashboard for you to publish or bin; listings edited in the dashboard are never checked. Checks set to \"Add to risk score\" only take effect once a Risk Threshold is entered below. Added by the Automated Listing Moderation for HivePress plugin."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:212
msgid "Verified Vendors"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:213
msgid "Skip checks for verified vendors"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:214
msgid "Listings from vendors you have marked as verified skip every check on this screen, including the submission limit below. To verify someone, edit them under Vendors in the WordPress dashboard and tick Verified."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:220
msgid "Submission Limit (listings per 24 hours)"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:221
msgid "How many new listings one vendor may add in any 24 hours; only live and waiting-for-review listings count, and editing an existing listing never does. Verified vendors are exempt if you have ticked the setting above. Leave empty for no limit."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:228
msgid "Blocked Keywords"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:229
msgid "Words or phrases that block a listing from being submitted, separated by commas or new lines. Matching is case-insensitive and matches <strong>inside</strong> longer words: blocking <code>class</code> also blocks <code>classic</code>, so use Blocked Patterns with <code>\\b</code> boundaries for whole words. The buttons under Blocked Patterns add ready-made starter lists to both boxes for you to review."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:230
msgid "cheap, cash in hand, WhatsApp me"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:237
msgid "Blocked Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:238
msgid "Advanced: regular expressions, <strong>one per line only</strong> (commas are regex syntax, so they do not separate patterns). No delimiters, case-insensitive, e.g. <code>\\bclass\\b</code> blocks the whole word only and <code>\\bcash\\s*only\\b</code> blocks \"cash only\" with any spacing; escape a literal ~ as <code>\\~</code>, and invalid patterns are skipped. Note WordPress strips angle brackets on save, so assertions containing &lt; cannot be used."
msgstr ""

#. translators: this is a regular-expression example; keep the backslashes as they are.
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:240
msgid "\\bcash\\s*only\\b"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:247
msgid "Disguised Spellings"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:248
msgid "Also catch blocked words disguised with symbols or accents"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:249
msgid "Re-checks your keywords and patterns against copies of the text with accents removed, invisible characters stripped and common leet substitutions reversed, so blocking <code>shit</code> also catches <code>sh1t</code> and <code>$hit</code>. A substitution that changes the word (like <code>f0ck</code>) still needs its own keyword or pattern. This never blocks a word you have not blocked yourself, but accented spellings of your blocked words do match: block <code>cafe</code> and <code>café</code> is blocked as well."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:255
msgid "Phone Numbers"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:256
msgid "Detects sequences of 9 to 14 digits with optional spaces, dashes, brackets or a leading +, e.g. <code>07123 456789</code>; prices, years, dates and IP addresses are not affected. Be aware that <strong>any</strong> other run of 9 to 14 digits also matches, including barcodes, ISBNs and long reference numbers: if your listings routinely carry those, choose \"Add to risk score\" rather than \"Block submission\"."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:257
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:266
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:275
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:284
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:293
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:302
#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:313
msgid "Disabled"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:264
msgid "Email Addresses"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:265
msgid "Detects anything shaped like an email address, e.g. <code>name@example.com</code>. Obfuscated forms (\"name at gmail dot com\") are not detected; add a Blocked Pattern for those if needed."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:273
msgid "Website Addresses"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:274
msgid "Detects links starting with http, https or www, plus bare domains ending in a common extension such as <code>example.com</code> or <code>example.co.uk</code>. Note this also applies to your own site address if vendors mention it."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:282
msgid "Duplicate Titles"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:283
msgid "Detects when another live or pending listing already has the same title, ignoring case and extra spaces. Existing listings are prepared automatically in the background, so on a large site an older listing may not be recognised for the first few minutes. If your site builds titles from attributes (the Title Format setting on this tab), vendors never type a title and this check stays quiet."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:291
msgid "Duplicate Descriptions"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:292
msgid "Detects when another live or pending listing already has an identical description, ignoring case, formatting and extra spaces. The match has to be exact: change one word and it is no longer spotted, so this catches copy-and-paste rather than rewriting."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:300
msgid "AI Text Review (OpenAI)"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:301
msgid "Sends the words in the listing (not the photos) to OpenAI's content checking service, which looks for hate, harassment, violence, self-harm and sexual content; it needs an OpenAI API key on the Integrations tab. The checks cost nothing, but OpenAI refuses every request on an account with no credit or payment method, and the listing text leaves your site, so say so in your privacy policy. If OpenAI cannot be reached the submission goes through unchecked, and a warning appears on this screen."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:309
msgid "AI Photo Review (OpenAI)"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:310
msgid "Checks listing photos (never videos) with the same OpenAI service, which flags sexual, violent and self-harm imagery; up to ten photos are checked per listing, and an OpenAI API key on the Integrations tab is required. The calls cost nothing, but OpenAI refuses every request on an account with no credit or payment method, and the photos leave your site, so say so in your privacy policy. If the service is unavailable the submission proceeds unchecked, and a warning appears on this screen."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:318
msgid "Excessive Capitals"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:319
msgid "Add shouty text to the risk score"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:320
msgid "Adds risk points when a field is written mostly in capitals (70% or more of at least 12 letters), e.g. \"BUY NOW CHEAP!!!\". This is a risk signal only, never an outright block, and only counts when a Risk Threshold is set below."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:326
msgid "Risk Threshold (points)"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:327
msgid "Every check set to \"Add to risk score\" adds points, and a listing whose total reaches this number is accepted but held as Pending for you to approve instead of going live: a lower number holds more listings, a higher number fewer, and a listing is never deleted automatically. Points per check: phone number 25, email address 25, website address 15, excessive capitals 15, duplicate title 40, duplicate description 40, AI text flag 50, AI photo flag 50; a good starting point is 20, so one contact detail or one duplicate is enough to hold a listing. Leave empty to switch scoring off entirely."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:338
msgid "Removing Automated Listing Moderation"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:339
msgid "Whatever the WordPress delete warning says, deleting this plugin keeps your settings and moderation records unless the box below is ticked, so you can reinstall later and carry on where you left off. Deactivating never removes anything."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:344
msgid "Data Removal"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:345
msgid "Delete all data when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:346
msgid "Tick this only if deleting the plugin should permanently remove every Automated Moderation setting, stored risk score and duplicate-detection record; this cannot be undone. The shared OpenAI API key is kept either way, because other extensions may use it."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:363
msgid "Your OpenAI connection, shared by any plugin on this site that uses OpenAI, so one key serves them all; Automated Listing Moderation uses it for the optional AI text and photo checks under Settings > Listings. Those checks cost nothing to run, but OpenAI refuses every request until the account has a payment method or purchased credit on it."
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:376
msgid "API Key"
msgstr ""

#: listing-moderation-for-hivepress.php:377
msgid "Only needed if you switch on AI text or photo review under Settings > Listings; create a key in the API keys section of <a href=\"https://platform.openai.com/api-keys\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">platform.openai.com</a> and paste it here. The checks cost nothing, but OpenAI allows no request at all until the account has a payment method or purchased credit. If the connection ever stops working, a warning appears on the Listings tab."
msgstr ""

